"""
Skeleton of a small tanker: how the hull, the tanks, the ballast circuit, the power
plant, the propeller and the rudder of this library come together in one ship.

It is `PoweredSingleScrewShip` (sample hull, hydrodynamics, propeller, rudder, free
propeller shaft) with the hull body reduced to a lightship mass, plus:

| Member | Component | What it is here |
|---|---|---|
| `cargo_1`, `cargo_2`, `cargo_3` | `FuelTank` | three centre cargo tanks, liquid mass `cargo_mass` each, no flow |
| `fore_peak`, `aft_peak` | `FuelTank` | two ballast tanks, liquid mass `peak_ballast_mass` each, no flow |
| `tank_a`, `tank_b`, pumps, valves | `AntiHeelingCircuit` | two wing ballast tanks (port, starboard) joined by a pump-and-valve circuit; `flow_cmd` and `direction` are set by the extender |
| `bunker` | `FuelTank` | fuel tank drained by the fuel rates of the plant's engines |
| `plant` | `DieselMechanicalPlant` | main engine through a gear to the propeller, generating set and hotel load on a bus |

Every tank is a `VariableMass` on the hull: its liquid adds weight, inertia and the lever
arm of its centre (at half the liquid height) to the multibody hull, so draft, trim and
heel follow the loading. `liquid_mass` is the sum over all tanks and `total_mass` adds
the hull body.

What the tank models cannot represent: a free surface (the liquid does not shift when
the ship heels, so there is no free-surface loss of stability), sloshing, tank shapes
other than a prism, pressure or temperature of the cargo, cargo pumping (the cargo and
peak tanks have no pipes; their rate input is held at zero) and flooding of a
compartment. Compartments that are not tanks would be further `VariableMass` or `Body`
elements on the same frame.

**Synthetic.** The hull is the library's 100 m sample hull, not a tanker hull; the
lightship mass, tank positions, sizes and fillings are round numbers chosen so that the
loaded ship floats near the sample hull's design draft. Extending components set the
orders: `plant.shaft_speed_order`, `plant.hotel_power_demand`, `rudder_order`,
`flow_cmd` [m³/h] and `direction` (+1 port to starboard, -1 the reverse).
"""
partial component TankerSkeleton
  extends PoweredSingleScrewShip
  extends AntiHeelingCircuit
  "Liquid mass in each of the three cargo tanks [kg]"
  parameter cargo_mass::Mass = 900e3
  "Liquid mass in each of the two peak ballast tanks [kg]"
  parameter peak_ballast_mass::Mass = 0
  "Fuel mass in the bunker tank at the start [kg]"
  parameter bunker_mass::Mass = 150e3
  cargo_1 = FuelTank(r_tank = [30, 0, 1.5], m0 = cargo_mass, rho = 850, A_tank = 192, H = 6)
  cargo_2 = FuelTank(r_tank = [50, 0, 1.5], m0 = cargo_mass, rho = 850, A_tank = 192, H = 6)
  cargo_3 = FuelTank(r_tank = [70, 0, 1.5], m0 = cargo_mass, rho = 850, A_tank = 192, H = 6)
  fore_peak = FuelTank(r_tank = [92, 0, 1], m0 = peak_ballast_mass, rho = 1025, A_tank = 120, H = 6)
  aft_peak = FuelTank(r_tank = [8, 0, 1], m0 = peak_ballast_mass, rho = 1025, A_tank = 120, H = 6)
  bunker = FuelTank(r_tank = [18, 0, 1], m0 = bunker_mass, rho = 900, A_tank = 50, H = 4)
  plant = DieselMechanicalPlant()
  "Liquid mass in all tanks [kg]"
  variable liquid_mass::Mass
  "Hull body plus all liquids [kg]"
  variable total_mass::Mass
relations
  connect(ship.frame_a, cargo_1.frame_a, cargo_2.frame_a, cargo_3.frame_a, fore_peak.frame_a, aft_peak.frame_a, bunker.frame_a, hull)
  connect(plant.propeller_flange, shaft.spline_a)
  cargo_1.Fuel_rate = 0
  cargo_2.Fuel_rate = 0
  cargo_3.Fuel_rate = 0
  fore_peak.Fuel_rate = 0
  aft_peak.Fuel_rate = 0
  bunker.Fuel_rate = plant.main_engine_fuel_mass_rate + plant.genset_fuel_mass_rate
  liquid_mass = cargo_1.mass + cargo_2.mass + cargo_3.mass + fore_peak.mass + aft_peak.mass + bunker.mass + mass_a.mass + mass_b.mass
  total_mass = hull_mass + liquid_mass
end

"""
Laden condition of the tanker skeleton (synthetic round numbers): lightship 2500 t,
three cargo tanks at 900 t each (92 % full at 850 kg/m³), peak ballast tanks empty, wing
ballast tanks 45 % full (46 t each), 150 t of fuel. Total 5442 t, which the sample
hull's hydrostatics carry at a draft of about 3.86 m.
"""
partial component TankerLaden
  extends TankerSkeleton(hull_mass = 2500e3, cargo_mass = 900e3, peak_ballast_mass = 0, ini_draft = 3.86)
end

"""
Ballast condition of the tanker skeleton (synthetic round numbers): lightship 2500 t,
cargo tanks at 20 t each (residue), peak ballast tanks at 700 t each (95 % full), wing
ballast tanks 45 % full, 150 t of fuel. Total 4202 t, a draft of about 3.05 m.
"""
partial component TankerBallast
  extends TankerSkeleton(hull_mass = 2500e3, cargo_mass = 20e3, peak_ballast_mass = 700e3, ini_draft = 3.05)
end

"""
Speed trial of the laden tanker: constant 80 rpm shaft order, 400 kW hotel demand,
rudder amidships, no ballast transfer.
"""
test component TankerLadenTrial
  extends TankerLaden(U0 = 5)
relations
  plant.shaft_speed_order = 80
  plant.hotel_power_demand = 400e3
  rudder_order = 0
  flow_cmd = 0
  direction = 1
end

analysis TankerLadenTrialTransient
  extends TransientAnalysis(stop = 600.0)
  model = TankerLadenTrial()
end

"""
The same speed trial in the ballast condition.
"""
test component TankerBallastTrial
  extends TankerBallast(U0 = 5)
relations
  plant.shaft_speed_order = 80
  plant.hotel_power_demand = 400e3
  rudder_order = 0
  flow_cmd = 0
  direction = 1
end

analysis TankerBallastTrialTransient
  extends TransientAnalysis(stop = 600.0)
  model = TankerBallastTrial()
end

"""
Ballast transfer under way in the ballast condition: between `t_on` and `t_off` the
circuit pumps from the port wing tank to the starboard one at the pump's nominal rate.
The water moved follows the pump characteristic and the valve losses; the ship heels
towards the tank that fills, and the total liquid mass changes only by the fuel burnt.
"""
test component TankerBallastTransfer
  extends TankerBallast(U0 = 5)
  parameter t_on::Time = 100
  parameter t_off::Time = 400
relations
  plant.shaft_speed_order = 80
  plant.hotel_power_demand = 400e3
  rudder_order = 0
  flow_cmd = ifelse(time > t_on, ifelse(time < t_off, 200, 0), 0)
  direction = 1
end

analysis TankerBallastTransferTransient
  extends TransientAnalysis(stop = 900.0, tstops = [100.0, 400.0])
  model = TankerBallastTransfer()
end
